==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|derely}}, {{m|enm|deorliche}}, from {{inh|en|ang|dēorlīċe|t=worthily, richly}}, equivalent to {{af|en|dear|-ly}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈdɪɹli/|a=GenAm}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈdɪəli/|a=RP}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-dearly.ogg|a=US}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv|more|er|comp2_qual=rare|sup2_qual=rare}}

# In a dear or precious manner.
#: {{ux|en|the funeral of our '''dearly''' beloved sister}}
# In a [[dear]] or expensive manner.
#: {{ux|en|a '''dearly''' priced item}}
# At great [[expense]].
#: {{ux|en|He paid '''dearly''' for his mistake.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=John Poulos|title=Dominion’s C.E.O.: Why We Settled the Lawsuit Against Fox News|work=The New York Times|date=2023-04-21|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2023/04/21/opinion/dominion-ceo-fox-lawsuit.html|issn=0362-4331|passage= But I take solace in the fact that the public has seen the enormous mountain of evidence proving what Fox did, and Fox paid '''dearly''' for it.}}

